{#
  BeMart Shopping error page — EC-CUBE goShoppingError.

  PORT of EC-CUBE 4.3 default-theme `Shopping/shopping_error.twig`
  (src/Eccube/Resource/template/default/Shopping/shopping_error.twig).

  DATA page (see var/templates/README.md). Markup skeleton, the
  `ec-role` / `ec-pageHeader` / `ec-off3Grid` / `ec-off4Grid` /
  `ec-blockBtn--cancel` classes and the block structure are kept
  verbatim from EC-CUBE.

  EC-CUBE-ism rebinding (see var/templates/README.md):
   - `{{ 'key'|trans }}` -> the ja literal from messages.ja.yaml.
   - `{{ include('Shopping/alert.twig', {'error_only': true}) }}` —
     EC-CUBE's alert partial iterates `app.session.flashbag` to surface
     the underlying error reason (stock / payment / session). BeMart has
     no flashbag transport (the Error resource is a Wave 3H pure
     renderer — see src/Resource/Page/Shopping/Error.php), so the
     include is OMITTED; with an empty flashbag EC-CUBE's alert partial
     also emits nothing, so it contributes nothing to the render diff.
     Surfacing the actual error reason is a MISSING BODY FIELD
     follow-up (a flashbag-equivalent error transport).
#}
{% extends 'base.html.twig' %}

{% set body_class = 'cart_page' %}
{% set route = 'shopping-error' %}
{% set title = '購入エラー' %}

{% block main %}

<div class="ec-role">
    <div class="ec-pageHeader">
        <h1>購入エラー</h1>
    </div>
</div>

<!-- アラートメッセージ -->

<div class="ec-role">
    <div class="ec-off3Grid">
        <div class="ec-off3Grid__cell">
            <div class="ec-off4Grid">
                <div class="ec-off4Grid__cell">
                    <a class="ec-blockBtn--cancel" href="/cart">カートに戻る</a>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
{% endblock %}
